  "bodyText": "Log in\nBack to search\nSave\nShare\nNew units available\n4.5\nFabulous\n(21)\nBase rent\nAsk for pricing\nBeds\n1-3 Beds\nBaths\n1-2\nViridian\n1783 West 14th Avenue, Vancouver, BC\nView on map\nRequest a tour\nSelect a date to start scheduling a tour.\nLoading...\nFloor plans\nUpdated today\nThis listing displays base rent, which is the rent provided by the property and may not include recurring monthly fees and costs. Contact the property for more information. Show more\nAll\n1 Bed\n2 Beds\n3+ Beds\nOne Bedroom\n1 Bed / 1 Bath\nAsk for pricing\nFloor plan details\nUnit\tBase rent\tAvailability\t\n0405\tAsk for pricing\t\nNow\n\t\nView\nApply now\nJunior One Bedroom\n1 Bed / 1 Bath\nAsk for pricing\nFloor plan details\nUnit\tBase rent\tAvailability\t\n1008\tAsk for pricing\t\nNow\n\t\nView\nApply now\n\n1208\tAsk for pricing\t\nSep 30\n\t\nView\nApply now\nTwo Bedroom\n2 Beds / 1 Bath\nAsk for pricing\nFloor plan details\n\nCheck for available units\n\nContact us\nTwo Bedroom\n2 Beds / 2 Baths\nAsk for pricing\nFloor plan details\n\nCheck for available units\n\nContact us\nThree Bedroom\n3 Beds / 2 Baths\nAsk for pricing\nFloor plan details\n\nCheck for available units\n\nContact us\nRatings and reviews\n4.5\nFabulous\n21 Reviews\nParking\n3.5\nAmenities\n4.5\nMaintenance\n5.0\nStaff\n4.5\nValue\n4.0\nLocation\n5.0\nNoise\n5.0\nAnonymous\nVerified Resident\nJun 1, 2025\n\nGood place, noise is neighbour dependent, overpriced per square foot compared to other options\n\nAnonymous\nVerified Resident\nApr 29, 2025\n\nWe are happy to live here with some new faces and friendly neighbors that makes the community harmony.\n\nAnonymous\nVerified Resident\nMar 10, 2025\n\nWe're very happy with the staff and building.\n\nAnonymous\nVerified Resident\nDec 31, 2024\n\nThe building is nice at face value. But even in the 2 bedroom units, 750 sq. feet for nearly $4,000/ month (including parking and fees) is ridiculous and not sustainable for the long-term. The amount of square footage requires a lot of compromise in day-to-day living. The lack of closing doors on the master bedroom area, further adds to the lack of division between areas. The rent increase this year made me want to move out. Even though we collectively make over $250,000 per year, the value does not feel worthwhile. There is not enough space to justify the cost, especially since the avg. rates of rent have gone down over the past year in Vancouver.\n\nShow more\nMaria S.\nVerified Resident\nDec 16, 2024\n\nEverything is fine, great location and good maitenance\n\nGabryel\nVerified Resident\nDec 5, 2024\n\nWe have lived here since Viridian opened in 2020, love the building though would like to se e parking costs come down\n\nShow all 21 reviews\nReview this property\nNeighborhood\n\nUse the map to explore the neighborhood and see how it matches your interests.\n\n1783 West 14th Avenue, Vancouver, BC V6J 0H7\nTransit\nSchools\nSelf storage\nCoworking\nShops\nFood\nHealth\nLoading content, please wait...\nWalk Score®: 91, Transit Score®: 70, Bike Score®: 96\nLoading...\nContact information\nProperty managed by:\nBGO Living\nCall leasing office:\n(778) 786-0079\nProperty office hours:\nToday 9:00AM-5:00PM\nView all hours\nExplore popular searches\nBy bedroom count\nStudio apartments in Vancouver\n1-bedroom apartments in Vancouver\n2-bedroom apartments in Vancouver\n3-bedroom apartments in Vancouver\n4-bedroom apartments in Vancouver\nBy budget\nApartments under $600 in Vancouver\nApartments under $700 in Vancouver\nApartments under $800 in Vancouver\nApartments under $900 in Vancouver\nApartments under $1,000 in Vancouver\nShow more\nBy lifestyle & amenities\nPet friendly apartments in Vancouver\nFurnished apartments in Vancouver\nUtilities included apartments in Vancouver\nShort term rentals in Vancouver\nLuxury apartments in Vancouver\nShow more\nExplore more rentals\nFrequently asked questions\nWhen were prices and availability for this property last updated?\